title: Ham test
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''Principle:'' Patient red cells are incubated in acidified serum, activating complement. In [[paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria|Paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria]], loss of CD55/CD59 makes cells susceptible to lysis (positive test).
* ''Role:'' Historical test; replaced by peripheral-blood flow cytometry for deficient glycosylphosphatidylinositol (GPI)-anchored proteins.

Sources: ASH SAP, 9th ed., ch. 14, pp. 165–166; [[Borowitz et al. 2010|https://doi.org/10.1002/cyto.b.20525]].
